  "description": "ZEWKAP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C3 H10 N1 1+,C160 H184 Gd9 O42 1-,C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.629-5.189 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.38-169.99°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula ((CH3)3NH)0.5[Gd9(L)16(μ3-OH)8(μ5-O)2](H2O)5. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ5-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
